## Supabase (auth + Pro — planned checkout)

- **Schema**: `20250301000000_init_profiles_subscriptions.sql` — `profiles`, `subscriptions`, `bkash_agreements`, `payment_transactions`; `20250302000000_security_rls_hardening.sql` — `saved_dossiers`, `custom_alerts`, explicit deny policies on billing writes.
- **Types**: `frontend/src/lib/database.types.ts` (keep in sync with migrations; regenerate with Supabase CLI when schema changes).
- **News + verified claims** stay in backend PostgreSQL; subscription/payment and user research metadata in Supabase.

## Product vocabulary

- **Headline clash / cluster** — Same story, different framings (cluster or story detail view)
- **Perspective** — `neutral` \| `establishment` \| `opposition` \| `international` (`frontend/src/lib/perspectives.ts`; **`spectrumTabEn`** / **`COVERAGE_SPECTRUM_TAB_ORDER`** for Left–Center–Right–International feed tabs)
- **Bias meter** — Source or cluster lean score
- **Rumor badge** — Low corroboration or speculative coverage (`is_rumor` on articles)
- **Blindspot** — Coverage gap on the **establishment** or **opposition** axis (`lib/blindspot.ts`: **`detectBlindspot`** on enriched article perspectives; **`/blindspot`** feed via **`getBlindspotStories`**; **`BlindspotBanner`** on story detail)
- **Partiality** — One or more perspective buckets still empty while the cluster has ≥2 articles (`lib/partiality.ts`: **`analyzePartiality`**, **`partialityBannerCopy`**); **`PartialityBanner`** on story detail, **`StoryPartialityTeaser`** on feed cards — not the same as blindspot (axis dominance vs missing buckets)
- **Anti-clickbait summary** — **`buildAntiClickbaitBullets`** (RSS-only); **`AntiClickbaitSummaryPanel`** on story detail; **`StoryFeedCard`** bullet list. Matrix row **`anti_clickbait_summary`** — product name “Quick summary from different sources” (UI panel title still mentions anti-clickbait)
- **Story topics** — **`story-topics.ts`** maps cluster **`category`** to home filter chips and card/detail topic labels (BN + EN)
- **Story coverage UI** — **`StoryCoverageDetails`** (counts, dominant lean %, last updated via **`coverageStats`**); **`StoryTabs`**: default **Coverage** tab (**`StoryArticleFeed`** spectrum filters), **Compare** (**`HeadlineClashTriptych`** + grouped headlines + **`HeadlineCompare`**), **Perspectives** (**`PerspectiveComparison`** with per-bucket headlines)
- **Verified claim** — User-submitted claim with AI verdict + analysis (`verified_claims`, `/verify/[slug]`)
- **Shorup Pro** — Pricing `subscription-plans.ts` (৳49/mo, ৳399/yr; **`getYearlyPlanSavings`** in **`PaywallModal`**). Matrix: `subscription-features.ts` — **`PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS`**: **`follow_story`** (UI gated), **`narrative_evolution_timeline`**, **`custom_topic_radar_alerts`** (matrix placeholders). **`/pro`** + **`PaywallModal`** (`featureId`). News/browse open to all. **Entitlements**: Supabase `subscriptions` via **`subscription-access.ts`** / **`GET /api/me/pro`**; **`NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`**. PayEurasia checkout planned, not wired.

## Quality bar

- Match existing naming and file layout; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Type hints on Python public functions; strict TypeScript on frontend
- Never commit secrets; backend env via `backend/app/core/config.py` and `backend/.env.example`; frontend via `frontend/.env.local` (API URL, optional Supabase keys, optional `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`)
